                <pb facs="0450" n="348" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg348"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6338: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-29T10:00:00+08:00">May 29, 1933—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 29—12:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>485. Reuter from Canton, 28th: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Southwest Political Council has despatched telegram further accusing
                            Military Council of compromising with Japan as shown by recent truce in
                            North China. Southwest leaders ask whether Military Council in replacing
                            resistance with truce and withdrawing troops to Tangku and Tungchow,
                            stopping supply of arms to volunteers and forbidding boycott activities
                            had approval of the Central Executive Committee. If so these things not
                            only constitute violation of resolutions of Fourth Plenary Session of
                            the Central Executive Committee but are also contrary to wishes of the
                            people. If approval of Central Executive Committee was not obtained then
                            that body should mete out severe punishment to the official organ or
                            private individual who dared compromise with enemy and commit act of
                            selling the country.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
